{
  "$comment": "Conformance vectors for contracts/report-artifact.md. A READER must turn every case's `encoded` step list into its `resolved` snapshots. A WRITER must turn `resolved` back into `encoded` for cases marked direction 'both'; 'decode' cases are shapes a writer never produces but a reader must handle. A position omitted from a `resolved` step means the reader must produce no snapshot there. `objectCarrier` is separate: it is the `resultJson` shape, and a reader must order its entries by `seq` before resolving them. Copy this file rather than re-deriving the cases — both repos run it as a test.",
  "contractVersion": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "full-form passthrough",
      "why": "R3 — an artifact written before this contract (schemaVersion 2) reads unchanged, with no version negotiation.",
      "direction": "decode",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta",
            "fileId": 42
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta",
            "fileId": 42
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "delta chain from an empty state",
      "why": "The first step's delta carries the whole store; later steps carry only what changed. There is no separate baseline field.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "user": "a@example.com",
              "env": "beta"
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "fileId": 42
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "fileId": 43
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta",
            "fileId": 42
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta",
            "fileId": 42
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "env": "beta",
            "fileId": 43
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "explicit removal",
      "why": "R5 — a variable that goes away is read from `removed`, never inferred from its absence in `set`.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 1,
              "b": 2
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "removed": [
              "b"
            ]
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "c": 3
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1,
            "c": 3
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "empty delta versus absent field",
      "why": "R4 — `{}` means a snapshot was taken and nothing changed; an absent field means no snapshot was taken, and the reader must render nothing rather than the last known state.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 1
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1"
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 2
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1"
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "one position only",
      "why": "The two positions are independent; a step may record `after` without `before`.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 1
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 2
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mixed forms — full snapshot resets the state",
      "why": "R3 — a merged report can combine shards written before and after this contract. The full snapshot replaces everything accumulated, so `fileId` must not survive it.",
      "direction": "decode",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "user": "a@example.com",
              "fileId": 42
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "b@example.com"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "b@example.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "role": "admin"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "fileId": 42
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "fileId": 42
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "b@example.com"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "b@example.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.2",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "b@example.com"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "b@example.com",
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "value shapes survive unchanged",
      "why": "Values are arbitrary JSON. A reader must not coerce, reorder, or flatten them, and a value reappearing identically is not re-recorded.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "count": 0,
              "flag": false,
              "missing": null,
              "list": [
                1,
                "two",
                {
                  "three": 3
                }
              ],
              "nested": {
                "a": {
                  "b": [
                    true
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "count": 1
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "count": 0,
            "flag": false,
            "missing": null,
            "list": [
              1,
              "two",
              {
                "three": 3
              }
            ],
            "nested": {
              "a": {
                "b": [
                  true
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "count": 0,
            "flag": false,
            "missing": null,
            "list": [
              1,
              "two",
              {
                "three": 3
              }
            ],
            "nested": {
              "a": {
                "b": [
                  true
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "count": 0,
            "flag": false,
            "missing": null,
            "list": [
              1,
              "two",
              {
                "three": 3
              }
            ],
            "nested": {
              "a": {
                "b": [
                  true
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "count": 1,
            "flag": false,
            "missing": null,
            "list": [
              1,
              "two",
              {
                "three": 3
              }
            ],
            "nested": {
              "a": {
                "b": [
                  true
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "capped values are plain strings",
      "why": "§7 — an oversized value is replaced by a string marker, never a truncated object. A reader renders it as-is and must not try to reconstruct it.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "transcript": "aaaaaaaa… [truncated, 41233 chars]",
              "exportedBuffers": "[truncated, 2182344 chars] {\"md\":{\"type\":\"Buffer\",\"data\":[35,35,32…"
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "transcript": "aaaaaaaa… [truncated, 41233 chars]",
            "exportedBuffers": "[truncated, 2182344 chars] {\"md\":{\"type\":\"Buffer\",\"data\":[35,35,32…"
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "transcript": "aaaaaaaa… [truncated, 41233 chars]",
            "exportedBuffers": "[truncated, 2182344 chars] {\"md\":{\"type\":\"Buffer\",\"data\":[35,35,32…"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown fields are ignored",
      "why": "R6 — a step object may carry fields a consumer does not recognize; they must not affect resolution.",
      "direction": "decode",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "description": "Click login",
          "status": "success",
          "someFutureField": {
            "anything": true
          },
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 1
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a step list starts from empty",
      "why": "R1 — this is the second attempt of a retried test. Its state does not inherit from the first attempt's list, so its opening delta carries the whole store again.",
      "direction": "both",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "user": "a@example.com",
              "attempt": 2
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "attempt": 2
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "user": "a@example.com",
            "attempt": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a key in both set and removed",
      "why": "R6 — a conforming writer never emits this, but the resolution must not depend on which member a reader happens to apply first: set is applied, then removed, so the removal wins.",
      "direction": "decode",
      "encoded": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {
            "set": {
              "a": 1,
              "b": 2
            }
          },
          "contextAfterDelta": {}
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBeforeDelta": {},
          "contextAfterDelta": {
            "set": {
              "b": 99,
              "c": 3
            },
            "removed": [
              "b"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "resolved": [
        {
          "stepId": "main.0",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "stepId": "main.1",
          "contextBefore": {
            "a": 1,
            "b": 2
          },
          "contextAfter": {
            "a": 1,
            "c": 3
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "objectCarrier": {
    "why": "R2 — `resultJson` is an object, and a consumer of it (the cloud) visits ids in its own order: merged with actionStepsMap, split by phase, rebuilt as a tree. `seq` is the recorded order, so sorting by it yields the step list the delta chain resolves against. Here the keys are deliberately out of order and `main.1.2` sits between `main.1` and `main.10`, where neither insertion order nor an id sort would put it.",
    "resultJson": {
      "main.10": {
        "seq": 3,
        "contextAfterDelta": {
          "set": {
            "stage": "done"
          }
        }
      },
      "main.1": {
        "seq": 1,
        "contextAfterDelta": {
          "set": {
            "stage": "opened"
          }
        }
      },
      "main.1.2": {
        "seq": 2,
        "contextAfterDelta": {
          "set": {
            "stage": "expanded"
          }
        }
      },
      "main.0": {
        "seq": 0,
        "contextBeforeDelta": {
          "set": {
            "user": "a@example.com"
          }
        },
        "contextAfterDelta": {}
      }
    },
    "expectedOrder": [
      "main.0",
      "main.1",
      "main.1.2",
      "main.10"
    ],
    "expectedResolved": [
      {
        "stepId": "main.0",
        "contextBefore": {
          "user": "a@example.com"
        },
        "contextAfter": {
          "user": "a@example.com"
        }
      },
      {
        "stepId": "main.1",
        "contextAfter": {
          "user": "a@example.com",
          "stage": "opened"
        }
      },
      {
        "stepId": "main.1.2",
        "contextAfter": {
          "user": "a@example.com",
          "stage": "expanded"
        }
      },
      {
        "stepId": "main.10",
        "contextAfter": {
          "user": "a@example.com",
          "stage": "done"
        }
      }
    ],
    "legacyNoSeq": {
      "why": "An artifact written before `seq` existed relied on key insertion order; a reader falls back to it when any entry lacks `seq`.",
      "resultJson": {
        "main.0": {},
        "main.1": {},
        "main.2": {}
      },
      "expectedOrder": [
        "main.0",
        "main.1",
        "main.2"
      ]
    }
  }
}
